<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean firms buy 20,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>S.Korean firms buy 20,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd jointly bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat on Wednesday from Japanese trading house Mitsubishi Corp, company officials said.  </p>
<p>Cheiljedang bought 8,300 tonnes at basis prices over July futures on the U.S grain futures exchanges including the Chicago Board of Trade, they said.</p>
<p>Dongah Flour purchased the remaining 11,700 tonnes at fixed prices.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for June 15-July 15 to the southeastern port of Pusan.</p>
